    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Crisp-skinned branzino, seared in ghee with lemon zest and finished in the oven, served over a silky swoosh of roasted butternut puree with a bright celery salad. Roast the squash first. The fish takes under 10 minutes, so cook it last.</p><p><em>“Celery leaves are one of the most underrated greens out there. Most people toss them, but they bring a bright, complex flavor that’s equal parts herbal, peppery and fresh. Every time I let them take center stage, they somehow still feel unexpected, and that’s exactly why I love making them the star of the show.”</em> &mdash; Miriam</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
