        "m_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Make the puree and the dressing up to 1 day ahead and refrigerate them. Rewarm the puree with a splash of olive oil. Slice the celery up to 2 hours ahead and keep it in ice water for extra crunch, then drain and pat it dry.</p><p>Thaw the branzino in the fridge overnight, and pat it very dry before it goes into the pan.</p>",
